# Build context for docker/Dockerfile.cpu and docker/Dockerfile.gpu is the
# repo root (they need ros_packages/, misc/robosuite, misc/robocasa,
# misc/robosuite_models). This trims everything else that isn't needed
# inside the image and would otherwise bloat the build context upload.
#
# Do NOT exclude misc/robosuite, misc/robocasa, or misc/robosuite_models
# themselves -- the Dockerfiles `pip install -e` them, so they must be
# present in the build context. Their large *downloaded data* subdirectories
# (RoboCasa's kitchen assets, its demo dataset cache) are excluded further
# below instead, since those are bind-mounted in at singularity/docker run
# time rather than baked into the image -- see
# docs/source/howto/running_on_cesga.md.

.git
.gitmodules

.venv/
ros_packages/build/
ros_packages/install/
ros_packages/log/

docs/build/
docs/_build/

**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

MUJOCO_LOG.TXT
.vscode/

# RoboCasa kitchen assets are intentionally NOT baked into the image (see
# docker/Dockerfile.cpu's header comment) -- bind-mounted in at run time
# instead. A *fresh* submodule checkout (CI) never has these populated, but
# a LOCAL `docker build` on a machine that already ran ./setup.sh will have
# ~10-25GB sitting under these paths; exclude them explicitly so a local
# build doesn't transfer all of it into the build context every time.
misc/robocasa/robocasa/models/assets/textures/
misc/robocasa/robocasa/models/assets/generative_textures/
misc/robocasa/robocasa/models/assets/fixtures/
misc/robocasa/robocasa/models/assets/objects/
# Local-only asset mirror some dev workflows populate under the ROS
# package itself (untracked by git; emdb_simulator's setup.py data_files
# only need assets/grippers/, not assets/robocasa/).
ros_packages/src/emdb_simulator/assets/robocasa/
# robocasa's own (gitignored-in-submodule, multi-GB) demonstration dataset
# cache -- not needed to install/build the package.
misc/robocasa/datasets/
